# glow — render markdown in the terminal

## Render
    glow README.md                  # render a file (auto-pages if long)
    glow                            # TUI file browser for the current dir
    glow ~/Documents/Tech\ Notes    # TUI browser for a dir
    glow github.com/charmbracelet/glow   # fetch + render a GitHub repo's README
    glow https://example.com/x.md   # render a remote file
    cat notes.md | glow -           # render from stdin

## Display flags
    -p / --pager                    # force pager (less-style scrolling)
    -t / --tui                      # force TUI mode for a file
    -w 100                          # word-wrap at width (0 disables)
    -s dark | light | dracula | pink | notty   # style (default: auto)
    -n / --preserve-new-lines       # keep single newlines
    -l / --line-numbers             # show line numbers (TUI only)
    -a / --all                      # include hidden files (TUI only)

## Config
    glow config                     # edit ~/.config/glow/glow.yml

## TUI keys
    j/k, ↑/↓   move          enter   open file       esc/q   back / quit
    /          filter files  e       edit in $EDITOR  r       refresh
    ?          full help
